\newlabel{fig:main}{{1}{3}{\textbf {Main result (restricted-context stress setting).} Deadline-qualified F1 (left) and miss rate (right) vs.\ deadline, 10 held-out HotpotQA questions, 150 runs on vLLM/A40. Dashed lines: miss rate predicted by the MDP from the calibration costs. RSS and the optimal MDP policy coincide in 29/30 question--deadline cells (points offset $\pm $0.12\,s for visibility). When on time, all policies give similar F1 (${\approx }0.77$): the gain is timeliness}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:preload}{{2}{3}{\textbf {KV preloading microbenchmark} (live server, prefix caching on, 30 requests). Left: latency of the final request after the last result arrives; preload requests (dashed) run while tools are still out. Right: fraction of the final prompt served from the prefix cache (server-reported \texttt {cached\_tokens})}{figure.2}{}}
